| Every enemy in the fight either dies or is reduced to 5% HP when the wearer dies...unless they're resistant to Kamikaze (like all bosses).
|}

All of these items are great...but require literal hours to get in the SNES version.  This all changes in the remakes.  They introduce a 100 coin slot machine in the center of the building, and allow you to invest up to 300 Tokens per row!  Plus, the maximum payout is now '''3,000,000 Coins'''!  

No, that was not a typo; the payouts are that absurdly high.  6000 Coin payouts, for example, are relatively common! 

The end result is this: It only takes around 14-38 minutes to get 27,000+ Coins, assuming optimal play.  So, it is recommended you purchase...

* 2x Platinum Mails
* 2x Dragon Shields
* 6x Yggdrasil Leaves
* 20x Silk Tuxedos
* Up to 20x Magic Waters

Firstly, the Platinum Mails and Dragon Shields are obscenely strong for this point in the game. Secondly, the Silk Tuxedos sell for 2625G apiece, guaranteeing that money will never be a problem.  Thirdly, the Magic Waters guarantee that you will never run out of MP again.  Finally, the Yggdrasil Leaves are an outstanding safety net, and you'll want at least 6x for the final boss 'anyway'.  You may as well get them now.

Now, you likely don't have enough assets to sell to get more than 200 Coins, but that's alright.  Just follow Methods 1-2 below; they're where the "14-38 minute" benchmark originated from Methods 1 and 2.  It is unknown whether Methods 3 and 4 can deliver results as consistently as the former two.

== Method 1  ==

# Buy 210+ Coins, and keep betting 70 Coins per spin on the 10 Coin slot machines.  Save your game for every time you gain more Coins, and Reset if you ever run out.  Keep doing this until you have gotten 600 Coins.
# Start betting 300 Coins per spin on the 100 Coin slot machine now.  Do the same thing as you did in step 1, and be sure to increase the amount of Coins you spend as you keep gaining more and more.  In general, you should always spend enough Coins so that you will run out after just 3 bad spins.  Do this until you have gotten to 6000 Coins.
# Only save after you get 2000 more Coins than you had before, and start resetting every time you lose 6000 Coins or more. The "4 Blue Fruit" line-up is the last high paying line-up to have a reasonable chance of showing up per spin, and it gives that exact amount; if you've gotten to the point where even that cannot recoup your losses, you're better off just restarting.

== Method 2 ==

{{Quote|Get at least 200 Coins (300 is preferred), and keep betting it all, each and every spin.  Save after every time you get at least 900 more Coins than what you started with.  Once you get 6000 Coins or more, save whenever you win enough to increase your starting funds by 20%, and reset whenever you end up having 6000 Coins than you started with.  Do not let your Coins fall below 2700 before leaving; you start winning Coins much faster when you're able to bet 900 Coins three times before having to reset.|Made by HCBailly|Paraphrased by Fionordequester}}

== Method 3 ==

{{Quote|Afford 100 Tokens minimum (200 is preferred, but 100 is sufficient).  SAVE, then enter the Port Haven Slots and bet on the 1-Token slot machines.  Play until earnings hit 800 - 1,000 Tokens.  If everything is lost, reset.  If not, SAVE again.  Next, return to the Port Haven Casino and play the 10-Token Slots and play until 5,000 - 10,000 Tokens are won.  If everything is lost, reset.  If not, SAVE once more.  It is highly recommended to play while watching a movie, as luck can be poor and the process tedious, however this is usually not the case but luck can hold out for a bit and still be boring before big winnings come pouring in.  With that 5,000 to 10,000 Tokens, and the game SAVED, go back down to the Port Haven 100-Token slots.  This time watch a movie and play until winnings are at least 50k.  Save once more, return and play until satisfied.|Provided by "BehindtheWord's" Gamefaqs Guide|Paraphrased by Fionordequester}}

